# [CompliRules] KVKK & Commercial Electronic Communication (ETK) Granular Consent and Pre-ticked Box Prohibition
**Severity:** `CRITICAL` | **Jurisdiction:** `KVKK_TR`

<!-- NOTICE: CompliRules provides automated AST guardrails without warranty (See DISCLAIMER.md). For certified pentests & DPO audits: https://halilyilmz.github.io/complirules/#partners -->

## Legal Citations
- **6698 Sayılı KVKK (Madde 3 & Md. 5 (Kurul İlke Kararı 2019/09))**: Açık rızanın belirli bir konuya ilişkin olması ve hizmet şartına bağlanamaması (Bundled Consent yasağı).
- **6563 Sayılı Elektronik Ticaretin Düzenlenmesi Hakkında Kanun (ETK) (Madde 6)**: Ticari elektronik ileti gönderimi için alıcının önceden onayının alınması (İYS uyumu).

## Rule Mandates
- MUST: Separate Privacy Policy / Terms acknowledgment from Commercial Marketing (ETK / İYS) consent into two distinct checkboxes.
- MUST: All consent checkboxes MUST be unchecked by default (`defaultChecked={false}`); pre-ticked checkboxes are strictly prohibited (Board Decision 2019/09).
- MUST: Service access (registration, purchase, newsletter) MUST NOT be conditioned upon granting commercial communication consent (Prohibition of Bundled Consent / KVKK Art. 5).
- MUST: Record explicit audit metadata for every consent granted: timestamp, consent version, IP address, and acceptance state in a `UserConsent` model.
- MUST: Provide an accessible opt-out mechanism within user settings allowing one-click withdrawal of consent at any time (KVKK Art. 11).

## Forbidden Anti-Patterns
- NEVER: <input type="checkbox" defaultChecked={true} /> on any consent or marketing checkbox
- NEVER: Bundling privacy policy and marketing consent into a single unified checkbox
- NEVER: Disabling the signup submit button until the user agrees to marketing emails
- NEVER: Sending promotional emails or SMS without an explicit opt-in timestamp logged in the database

